{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1517","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1517","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1517\",\"parent_revision\":\"33776d776d99fe29948b89ae487f816b64d37afa9f29ca83c15faa80dadd5b10\",\"root_revision\":\"33776d776d99fe29948b89ae487f816b64d37afa9f29ca83c15faa80dadd5b10\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ngithub_task.py and memory.py each hand-roll the get_plan_status aggregation: by_status counting, ready/blocked task extraction, completion_pct, has_cycles. LocalYamlTaskProvider correctly delegates this to query.get_plan_status. The duplication means three independent implementations of the same summary logic that must stay in sync. Extracting a shared TypedDict-aware aggregation function (or adapting query.get_plan_status to accept TaskData lists) would eliminate two copies.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n[VERIFIED] Three independent `get_plan_status` implementations exist.\\n\\n- `local_yaml.py:553-579` \u2014 `LocalYamlTaskProvider.get_plan_status` delegates to `query.get_plan_status(path)` at line 568, then unwraps the `PlanStatus` dataclass into a `dict`. No hand-rolled logic.\\n- `memory.py:522-569` \u2014 `InMemoryTaskProvider.get_plan_status` hand-rolls all aggregation: `by_status` counting (lines 541-545), ready/blocked extraction (lines 547-555), `completion_pct` (lines 557-559), and calls private `_has_cycle(tasks)` at line 568.\\n- `github_task.py:460-486` \u2014 `GitHubTaskProvider.get_plan_status` hand-rolls the same aggregation: `by_status` counting (lines 466-468), ready/blocked via `_is_ready` (lines 469-474), `completion_pct` (lines 476-477), and calls private `_has_cycles(tasks)` at line 485.\\n\\n[VERIFIED] `query.get_plan_status` (line 422, `query.py`) takes a `Path` and returns a `PlanStatus` typed model. It cannot accept a `list[TaskData]` directly \u2014 it must load a plan from disk. This makes direct reuse impossible for the GitHub and memory backends.\\n\\n[VERIFIED] The blocking type mismatch: `query.get_plan_status` calls `DependencyGraph(plan.tasks)` where `plan.tasks` is `list[Task]` (Pydantic). Both other backends operate on `list[TaskData]` (TypedDict). There is no existing shared aggregation function that accepts `TaskData`.\\n\\n[INCONCLUSIVE \u2014 minor divergence found] `github_task.py:472` blocked task detection uses `_is_ready` negation with a `t[\\\"dependencies\\\"]` guard, while `memory.py:551` uses `status_by_id.get(d, \\\"\\\") not in _TERMINAL_STATUSES`. These produce the same result but via different logic paths. No confirmed bug, but the divergence is a maintenance risk.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: refactor\\n\\nRoot cause: `query.get_plan_status` was designed for the file-based backend (takes a `Path`). When the GitHub and memory backends were added, no TypedDict-layer aggregation function existed, so each backend reimplemented the logic. The absence of a `_plan_status_from_task_data(feature: str, tasks: list[TaskData]) -> dict[str, object]` helper is the structural gap.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/memory.py:522-569` \u2014 hand-rolled aggregation to replace\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/github_task.py:460-486` \u2014 hand-rolled aggregation to replace\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/backends/local_yaml.py:553-579` \u2014 reference implementation (correct delegation pattern)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/query.py:422-461` \u2014 `query.get_plan_status` (Pydantic layer \u2014 not directly reusable but shows the expected output shape)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Three implementations must stay in sync. A change to `PlanStatus` semantics (e.g. adding a new key) requires three edits.\\n- Minor logic divergence between backends already exists (blocked task detection). If left unaddressed this will produce subtly different status outputs depending on which backend is active.\\n- `github_task.get_plan_status` also depends on the private `_has_cycles` being removed by #1516 \u2014 both issues share a fix boundary.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nBlocked on #1516: the shared aggregation function must call `_has_cycles_from_task_data` (produced by #1516). Implement #1516 first, or include both in the same PR.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] A module-level function `_aggregate_plan_status(feature: str, tasks: list[TaskData]) -> dict[str, object]` exists in a shared location with fully TypedDict-typed signature \u2014 no `cast()` over TypedDict, no `object` or `Any` parameter types.\\n- [ ] `InMemoryTaskProvider.get_plan_status` delegates to the shared function; the hand-rolled aggregation logic is removed from `memory.py`.\\n- [ ] `GitHubTaskProvider.get_plan_status` delegates to the shared function; the hand-rolled aggregation logic is removed from `github_task.py`.\\n- [ ] The shared function calls `_has_cycles_from_task_data` (resolved by #1516) for cycle detection \u2014 no inline cycle detection in the shared function.\\n- [ ] `LocalYamlTaskProvider.get_plan_status` is unchanged (it already delegates correctly via `query.get_plan_status`).\\n- [ ] The `dict[str, object]` return type of the shared function is consistent with what `LocalYamlTaskProvider.get_plan_status` already returns (same keys: `feature`, `total_tasks`, `by_status`, `ready_tasks`, `blocked_tasks`, `completion_pct`, `has_cycles`).\\n- [ ] Conformance tests verify all three backends return identical output for the same logical plan state.\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files <changed files>` exits 0.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: S\\nReasoning: Extract one shared function, update two call sites, add/update conformance tests. The logic already exists in three places \u2014 this is assembly and deduplication, not new algorithmic work. The #1516 dependency is small and can be bundled.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **get_plan_status aggregation duplicated in github_task.py and memory.py \u2014 should delegate to query module** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Simplify review of P912 \u2014 .tmp/scratch/reports/simplify-reuse-P912.md\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0c41576604054d9575ffeeb6e3ca44e88036365684e0434ec74aa1874fd7ff3e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdr8Yg\"}"}